# Workflow plan step C1 (docs/WORKFLOW_PLAN.md, 2026-11-14): CalculiX Setup in engineering words. The beam starter's Setup says
# what the model is (linear static, the mesh, metres-newtons-pascals), its material (steel, matched to the library), its
# support (FIXED, 25 nodes, held in x to z) and its load (40 N on each of TIP's 25 nodes: 1 kN in total). The total set to
# 2000 N writes 80 N a node; the material switched to aluminium writes its E and density; saved, the file runs in ccx.
action go.new
wait-until page New case
click new-prog:calculix
wait 5
click label:Cantilever beam
wait 5
click clone-name
key A ctrl
type c1beam
click clone-go
wait-until page Overview timeout 10
click nav:setup
wait-until page Setup
wait 10
assert text The model
assert text Linear static
assert text Material STEEL · Structural steel
assert text Support FIXED · 25 nodes
assert text Force on TIP · 25 nodes
assert text 40 N on each node along -z: 1000 N in total
screenshot $OUT/c1_model.png
click ccx-total#0
key A ctrl
enter 2000
wait 10
assert text 80 N on each node along -z: 2000 N in total
click ccx-mat#0
wait 3
click text:Aluminium 6061-T6
wait 10
assert text Material STEEL · Aluminium 6061-T6
click ps-save
wait 10
shell grep -q '^TIP, 3, -80$' $SB/home/calculix/c1beam/beam.inp && touch $OUT/load-ok
assert file $OUT/load-ok
shell grep -q '^6.89e+10, 0.33$' $SB/home/calculix/c1beam/beam.inp && grep -q '^2700$' $SB/home/calculix/c1beam/beam.inp && touch $OUT/mat-ok
assert file $OUT/mat-ok
screenshot $OUT/c1_saved.png
click nav:run
wait-until page Run
click run-go
wait-until job finished timeout 120
wait 20
assert text Finished
